[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Accelerated London System"]
[ECO "D00"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "bishop-outside,e5-outpost,kingside-attack"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "1...d5 2.Bf4 Nf6"]
[Start "london-bf4-first 2.Bf4"]

2... Nf6 3. e3 { Supports d4 and opens the other bishop. The c1 bishop is already outside the pawn chain, so this costs nothing. } 3... e6 ( 3... c5 4. Nd2 e6 ( 4... Nc6 5. c3 ) ( 4... cxd4 5. exd4 ) 5. c3 Nc6 6. Ngf3 ) ( 3... Bf5 4. Nf3 e6 ( 4... Nc6 5. c4 e6 ( 5... Nb4 6. Qa4+ { Check, and the queen also attacks the knight on b4. } 6... c6 7. Qxb4 ) 6. Nc3 { Transposes to 2...Nc6 3.e3 Bf5 4.c4 e6 5.Nc3 Nf6 6.Nf3. } ) ( 4... h6 5. c4 ) ( 4... a6 5. c4 ) 5. c4 ) ( 3... Nc6 { Transposes to 2...Nc6 3.e3 Nf6. } ) ( 3... g6 4. Nd2 Bg7 5. Ngf3 O-O 6. h3 { Gives the bishop h2, so ...Nh5 cannot chase it off the diagonal. } ) ( 3... Bg4 4. Nf3 e6 5. Nbd2 ) ( 3... a6 4. Nd2 ) ( 3... c6 4. Nd2 ) 4. Nd2 { Heads for f3 and leaves the c-pawn free to support d4. It also sets a small trap: if Black's knight jumps to h5 to hit the bishop, Qxh5 wins it. } 4... c5 ( 4... Be7 5. Bd3 ) ( 4... Nc6 { Transposes to 2...Nc6 3.e3 Nf6 4.Nd2 e6. } ) ( 4... Bb4 5. c3 ) ( 4... Bd6 5. Bg3 { The bishop steps back to g3. If Black trades on g3, the h-pawn recaptures and the h-file opens for later. } 5... O-O ( 5... Bxg3 6. hxg3 ) 6. Ngf3 c5 7. c3 Nc6 8. Bd3 ) 5. c3 { Backs up d4, so after ...cxd4 White recaptures with a solid centre and nothing hangs. } 5... Nc6 ( 5... cxd4 6. exd4 ) ( 5... Bd6 6. Bg3 ) ( 5... Qb6 6. Qb3 { Offers a queen trade, which removes the attacker of b2. If Black avoids it with ...c4, Qxb6 axb6 leaves doubled b-pawns. } 6... Nc6 7. Ngf3 ) 6. Ngf3 Bd6 ( 6... Be7 7. Bd3 ) ( 6... cxd4 7. exd4 ) ( 6... Qb6 7. Qb3 ) ( 6... a6 7. Bd3 ) 7. Bg3 { Keeps the bishop instead of trading it. From g3 it still eyes the e5 square, and a trade on g3 would open the h-file for White. } 7... O-O ( 7... Bxg3 8. hxg3 ) 8. Bd3 { Points at h7 and clears the back rank so White can castle. } 8... b6 9. Ne5 { The knight can sit here for good: the d4 pawn supports it and no black pawn can kick it away. } 9... Bb7 10. O-O { Castle before starting the attack. Next come f4 and Qf3 or Qe2, with the knight on e5 as the anchor. When Black leaves the book, aim for Ne5, f4 and a kingside attack. } *
